suppliesRequired:
Baseline (always): reclaimed and tactile materials (cardboard, timber offcuts, fabric, clay, salvaged street furniture), basic hand tools and fixings (tape, zip-ties, rope, scissors, saws), markers, and a simple ground cover/base to define the installation footprint.

Register-dependent (pick with the artist):

tactile-material → extra raw/scrap materials, moldable media (clay, plaster);
ephemeral-performative → chalk, textiles, lightweight structures, simple sound/light;
cartographic-narrative → large canvas/paper, transparent overlays, photos, pens;
sensory-ecological → plants, soil, natural elements, aromatic/tactile species;
playful-ludic → modular blocks, cards, movable props.

Observation & documentation: camera/phone, notebook or observation prompt cards, and something to log changes over time.

Site & safety: permissions/host presence to signal the space may be used and altered, plus basic safety gear if building on site.
